  "aiContextParagraph": "A wave of endorsements has emerged for Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, the current Deputy Speaker of the Indonesian House of Representatives, to fill the role of Vice President. Regional branches of the Gerindra Party, including those in Jambi, Bangka Belitung, North Sulawesi, and South Sulawesi, have formally expressed support for his candidacy. The momentum has extended beyond the internal party structure, with additional backing from other political figures and organizations. Supporters highlight his aptitude for political strategy and his history of facilitating the implementation of presidential programs. Furthermore, high-level political leaders have reportedly reached a consensus that the next occupant of the Vice President office should be a member of the Gerindra Party. Analysts suggest these developments solidify his position as a prominent figure in discussions surrounding the succession, emphasizing his perceived capability to navigate complex political landscapes and provide solutions for national governance.",
